      "arm_key": "cognitive_biases::curiosity_trigger::evening",
      "text_sha": "157e7395023c6e9470b78176fbeca11296e9478d27cf8bd949e53d18cd5cce0f",
      "text": "How Confirmation Bias Controls Your Opinions There's a word manipulators are terrified you'll learn. You've felt it before — that quiet discomfort you couldn't explain. Here's what it was. Research into human behavior confirms it: familiarity breeds acceptance. The more you hear something, the more true it feels. What makes it dangerous is how ordinary it looks. But now that you've seen it, you'll start noticing it everywhere. Follow Cognitive Dark for the psychology they don't teach you in school.",
      "source": "template",
      "run_id": "20260804T230645",
      "ts": "2026-08-04T23:11:15.885683+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "The Cycle of Abuse You Keep Repeating | Dark Psychology Facts",
      "hook": "The Cycle of Abuse You Keep Repeating",
      "pillar": "red_flags",
      "hook_style": "counterintuitive",
      "arm_key": "red_flags::counterintuitive::morning",
      "text_sha": "48ce4eb6f26d1f86fd5b509e8ffb536d0b1c9a9bfa79db0c1b4c757553de311b",
      "text": "The Cycle of Abuse You Keep Repeating The trait you think is kindness is actually your weakness. Psychologists have studied this pattern for decades. Here's what they found. A landmark study on this pattern found it works in under ten seconds. That's faster than you can catch yourself. And that's the part nobody tells you: it doesn't need your permission. It just needs your attention. Follow Cognitive Dark — the dark side of the human mind, decoded daily.",
